ndled nose test suite\n  (equivalent to `python -m mordred.tests`).\n- `mo…)
ALEMBIC_EVENT {"type": "tool_call", "stage": "explorer", "name": "write_report", "args": {"report_name": "exploration", "content": "# mordred\n\n## Description\nmordred is a molecular descriptor calculator that computes ~1826\nchemoinformatics descriptors (1613 2D + 213 3D) for organic molecules given as\nRDKit `Mol` objects, SMILES, or SDF/MOL files. It is built on top of RDKit and\nNetworkX, exposes both a Python API (`Calculator(descriptors)(mol)`,\n`calc.pandas(mols)`, `calc.map(mols)`) and a CLI (`python -m mordred input.smi`),\nand ships a reference dataset (`mordred/tests/references/structures.sdf/.smi`,\n19 named molecules) plus YAML reference values used by its self-test suite.\n\n## Key files & workflows\n- `mordred/__init__.py` — public API: `Calculator`, `Descriptor`, `Result`,\n  `descriptors`, `is_missing`, `get_descriptors_in_module`.\n- `mordred/_base/calculator.py` — `Calculator` class. Key methods:\n  - `__init__(descs=None, version=None, ignore_3D=False, config=None)`\n  - `register(desc, version=None, ignore_3D=False)`\n  - `__call__(mol, id=-1)` → `Result` (one descriptor value per registered descriptor)\n  - `map(mols, nproc=None, nmols=None, quiet=False, ipynb=False, id=-1)` → iterator of `Result`\n  - `pandas(mols, nproc=None, nmols=None, quiet=False, ipynb=False, id=-1)` → `MordredDataFrame`\n  - `descriptors` property → tuple of registered `Descriptor` instances\n  - `to_json()` / `from_json(obj)` / `register_json(obj)`\n- `mordred/descriptors/__init__.py` — auto-imports all 50 descriptor modules;\n  `descriptors.all` is the tuple of all descriptor modules; `descriptors.<Name>`\n  (e.g. `descriptors.ABCIndex`) is each module.\n- `mordred/__main__.py` — CLI. `main(args=None)` parses argv and calls\n  `main_process(...)`. Supports `-t {auto,sdf,mol,smi}`, `-o OUTPUT`,\n  `-p PROCESSES`, `-q`, `-s` (stream), `-d DESC` (repeatable, picks a\n  descriptor module like `ABCIndex`), `-3` (3D), `-v` (verbosity).\n- `mordred/tests/__main__.py` — `main()` runs the bundled nose test suite\n  (equivalent to `python -m mordred.tests`).\n- `mordred/tests/test_by_references.py` — loads\n  `mordred/tests/references/structures.sdf` and compares computed descriptors\n  against YAML references in `mordred/tests/references/**/*.yaml`\n  (uses `numpy.testing.assert_almost_equal` with per-test `digit` precision).\n- `mordred/tests/test_ABCIndex.py` — reference values from\n  doi:10.2298/JSC150901093F; asserts `ABCIndex()`/`ABCGGIndex()` of\n  `CC(C)CCCCCCC` ≈ 6.58 / 6.49 (2 digits).\n- `mordred/tests/test_mordred_main.py` — exercises the CLI: writes\n  `c1ccccc1 Benzene` to `input.smi`, runs the CLI, asserts the output row has\n  `Nd2D` fields and the name column equals `Benzene`.\n- Bundled reference molecules: `mordred/tests/references/structures.smi`\n  (Hexane, Benzene, Caffeine, Cyanidin, Lycopene, Epicatechin, Limonene,\n  Allicin, Glutathione, Digoxin, Capsaicin, EllagicAcid, Astaxanthin, DMSO,\n  DiethylThioketone, VinylsulfonicAcid, Thiophene, Triethoxyphosphine,\n  MethylphosphonicAcid, MethylCyclopropane) and `structures.sdf` (same set\n  with 3D coordinates).\n\n## Environment\n- `setup.py` — `install_requires`: `six==1.*`, `numpy==1.*`, `networkx==2.*`\n  (+ `enum34` for Python < 3.4). `tests_require`: `nose==1.*`, `PyYaml>=4.2b1`.\n  `extras_require[\"full\"]`: `pandas`, `tqdm`.\n- RDKit is a hard runtime dependency (imported everywhere) but is NOT in\n  `install_requires` — the README instructs to install RDKit separately\n  (`conda install -c rdkit ...` or `pip install rdkit`).\n- No declared Python version pin; supports Python 2.7 + 3.x.\n- System libs: RDKit typically pulls in OpenGL libraries at install time.\n- Conda recipe `extra/requirements/requirements-conda.txt` lists:\n  `networkx six numpy tqdm pandas pyyaml nose pep8 isort flake8 coverage\n  coveralls sphinx conda-build anaconda-client`.\n- No pretrained weights — mordred is deterministic; it ships only small atomic\n  property tables in `mordred/data/*.txt` (mass, electronegativity,\n  polarizability, van-der-Waals radii, McGowan volume, ionization potential).\n\n## Test evidence\n- README: `Calculator(descriptors, ignore_3D=True)` → 1613 descriptors;\n  `Calculator(descriptors, ignore_3D=False)` → 1826 descriptors (1613 + 213 3D).\n- README: `calc(Chem.MolFromSmiles('c1ccccc1'))[:3]` →\n  `[4.242640687119286, 3.9999999999999996, 0]` (ABCIndex, ABCGG, nBase for\n  benzene).\n- README: `calc.pandas(['c1ccccc1Cl','c1ccccc1O','c1ccccc1N'])['SLogP']` →\n  `2.3400, 1.3922, 1.2688` (chlorobenzene, phenol, aniline).\n- README CLI: `python -m mordred example.smi -d ABCIndex` →\n  `benzene,4.242640687119286,3.9999999999999996` /\n  `chlorobenzene,5.059137268047012,4.785854275382693`.\n- `mordred/tests/test_ABCIndex.py::test_ABC`: `ABCIndex()` of\n  `CC(C)CCCCCCC` ≈ 6.58 and `ABCGGIndex()` ≈ 6.49 (assert_almost_equal, 2\n  digits), and three more rows.\n- `mordred/tests/test_mordred_main.py::test_smi`: writing\n  `c1ccccc1 Benzene` to `input.smi` and running the CLI yields exitcode 0,\n  first data row's first field `Benzene`, and the header has `Nd2D` commas\n  (i.e. 1613 fields).\n- `mordred/tests/test_by_references.py` + `mordred/tests/references/**/*.yaml`:\n  computed descriptors of the 19 molecules in `structures.sdf` are compared\n  against stored reference values to a per-test decimal precision.\n\n## Plan\n\n```json\n{\n  \"env\": {\n    \"requirements_files\": [\"setup.py\", \"extra/requirements/requirements-conda.txt\", \"extra/requirements/requirements-pip.txt\"],\n    \"dependencies\": [\"six==1.*\", \"numpy==1.*\", \"networkx==2.*\", \"rdkit\", \"nose==1.*\", \"PyYaml>=4.2b1\", \"pandas\", \"tqdm\"],\n    \"system_libs\": [\"libgl1\", \"libxext6\", \"libxrender1\"],\n    \"weights\": []\n  },\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"calc_descriptors\",\n      \"target\": \"mordred._base.calculator:Calculator\",\n      \"purpose\": \"Calculate all (or a subset of) mordred descriptors for a single RDKit Mol and return the Result vector.\",\n      \"sample_args\": {\"smiles\": \"c1ccccc1\", \"ignore_3D\": true},\n      \"evidence\": \"README shows calc(Chem.MolFromSmiles('c1ccccc1'))[:3] == [4.242640687119286, 3.9999999999999996, 0]; len(Calculator(descriptors, ignore_3D=True).descriptors) == 1613.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"calc_descriptors_pandas\",\n      \"target\": \"mordred._base.calculator:Calculator.pandas\",\n      \"purpose\": \"Calculate descriptors for a list of RDKit Mols and return a pandas DataFrame (one row per molecule, one column per descriptor).\",\n      \"sample_args\": {\"smiles_list\": [\"c1ccccc1Cl\", \"c1ccccc1O\", \"c1ccccc1N\"], \"ignore_3D\": true},\n      \"evidence\": \"README shows calc.pandas(mols)['SLogP'] == [2.3400, 1.3922, 1.2688] for chlorobenzene/phenol/aniline; column count equals len(Calculator(descriptors).descriptors).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"run_mordred_cli\",\n      \"target\": \"mordred.__main__:main\",\n      \"purpose\": \"Run the mordred command-line interface on a SMILES/SDF/MOL input file and emit a CSV of descriptor values.\",\n      \"sample_args\": {\"args\": [\"mordred/tests/references/structures.smi\", \"-d\", \"ABCIndex\", \"-q\", \"-o\", \"-\"]},\n      \"evidence\": \"README: `python -m mordred example.smi -d ABCIndex` prints `benzene,4.242640687119286,3.9999999999999996` / `chlorobenzene,5.059137268047012,4.785854275382693`; test_mordred_main.py::test_smi asserts exitcode 0, row has Nd2D fields, first data field is the molecule name.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"run_mordred_tests\",\n      \"target\": \"mordred.tests.__main__:main\",\n      \"purpose\": \"Run mordred's bundled nose test suite (reference-value tests over structures.sdf plus module/unit tests).\",\n      \"sample_args\": {},\n      \"evidence\": \"mordred/tests/__main__.py defines main() invoking nose over the mordred and mordred._base packages with NOSE_WITH_DOCTEST=1; README documents `python -m mordred.tests`; test_by_references.py compares computed descriptors against YAML references for the 19 molecules in mordred/tests/references/structures.sdf.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n"}}
